## Business Interpretation

Threshold-based detection identifies violations of predefined business expectations, while statistical detection identifies behaviour that is unusual relative to recent historical patterns.

The results are intended to support investigation and risk analysis rather than automatically make operational decisions.

---

## Limitations

* Thresholds depend on predefined business rules.
* Statistical detection depends on the quality and availability of historical data.
* A z-score does not establish the cause of an anomaly.
* Detected anomalies require human investigation.
* The system is not intended for real-time monitoring or automated remediation.

